r">1165</span><span class="rf-text">Henry II’s invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> founders on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berwyn-range">Berwyn</a> mountains against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owain-gwynedd">Owain Gwynedd</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1218</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-worcester">Treaty of Worcester</a> confirms <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-the-great">Llywelyn the Great</a>’s dominance in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1267</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-montgomery">Treaty of Montgomery</a> recognises <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1282</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd</a> is killed near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilmeri">Cilmeri</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1284</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/statute-of-rhuddlan">Statute of Rhuddlan</a> turns Gwynedd into English shires</span></li></ol>
